# The contained-offender route for the extraspecial alternative

This alternate route selects the local group by minimal order before forming
its action, and constructs best subgroups inside the actual elementary
endpoints. It does not require the whole endpoints to be best offenders.
The modules below establish:

* genuine minimal selection and survival of the normal two-core in every
  intermediate outside overgroup;
* exact star-image lifts, simultaneous conjugation and edge-core placement;
* exhaustive conditional construction of an outside C-component, equality
  of its reduced overgroup with the already selected H, and (j)–(l);
* minimal local-action reconstruction, cross-centralization, and strong
  offending at a compatible symmetric endpoint, followed by a contained
  strong best offender placed using that endpoint's own edge;
* the normal actor generated by all best offenders, its faithful generated
  action, trivial two-core and actual SQTK cover, and, after H = LT, its
  generalized Fitting subgroup equal to the component image;
* strict span from the local Fitting theorem and the actual orthogonal
  fixed-plane calculation, without an assumed local commutator equality;
* construction of the actual terminal seed point and its stabilizer,
  exclusion of all nonbinary terminal models, and elimination by minimality
  and component orders of the binary generation alternative;
* the final S₈ middle-node contradiction, using the late actor to establish
  component membership and natural-plus-dual coordinates for the later
  offender, followed by its concrete point-core rank bound.

`EarlierLocal.exists_terminal_input` assembles minimal selection through
strong placement from enumerated earlier local conclusions, the uniform
geometric-family inputs and universal appendix implications. The initial
contained offender and the later strong best offender remain separate;
`StrongPlacement.late_offender` proves membership and offending for the
latter in the late actor.

`EarlierLocal.false_of_earlier` completes the conditional extraspecial
contradiction: it selects the minimal H and constructs every offender,
component and terminal point before exhausting the models. It also derives
the seed quotient's order from the actual orthogonal fixed plane. The
enumerated uniform earlier local/F.9 and appendix implications remain with
the source parent for discharge. Thus this is the full conditional exclusion,
not a claim that all numbered conclusions of 15.3.49 are already assembled.
No legacy whole-endpoint bestness or component-product premise is used.

Final assembly is retained in this module. Source: Aschbacher–Smith,
combined manuscript (1 March 2004), B.1.4(4), B.5.1, B.5.3–6 and proof of
15.3.49, printed pp.68–69, 99–105 and 1142–1145.
-/
